  "title": "DataAccessV1dot11",
  "description": "K-05 v1.11, a minor version of the data-access calls (T-1249, from T-1240's NEED and README open gap 55; QUESTIONS.md CQ-220; DL-499). It only adds to v1.10 (data-access.v1.10.schema.json, frozen and unchanged, referred to here, which refers on to v1.9 and through it to every earlier version down to v1): every v1.10 definition is here under its own name, by reference, and none changes, so every v1 to v1.10 exchange is a v1.11 exchange. Added: one read on the runtime side, readTurnParty, the handle's party for a turn (README item 52; runtime/src/turn/types.ts TurnDirectory.partyOf and TurnParty): from a handle's kind and address, its K-04 id, the business the turn's calls run under, the person and the zone its texts' dates resolve in, by the rule item 52 gives for each case, and businessUndecided wherever the rows do not give one business the handle may act for, so the turn fails closed and never runs under a business picked for it (CQ-220's lead note). It runs as rosie_job with no business scope, reads the primary uncached, writes nothing and reads K-04 v1's handles, person_handles, person_roles and businesses and K-23 v1's companies as migrated (0002, 0004, 0012, 0019) with the grants rosie_job holds, so no column, grant, index or migration is added. Not model-facing, so number and length limits are schema rules here. Owner: the architect.",
